# rust build output
crates/*/target/

# The text core is a library crate, so its lock is not committed. The desktop
# shell in src-tauri/ IS an application, so its lock IS committed: it is what
# pins the Tauri tree, and an unpinned tree is how a release build that worked
# yesterday stops working today. This distinction is the whole reason the rule is
# not a bare `Cargo.lock`.
crates/*/Cargo.lock

# generated by scripts/build-wasm.mjs
ui/vendor/textcore.js

# forgen build output
*.exe
*.obj
*.pdb
.forgen_cache/

# generated single-file interface, both variants.
#
# `build-ui.mjs` writes the first and `build-ui.mjs --core` writes the second,
# and both are declared resources in tauri.conf.json. Only the first was ignored:
# the core variant was committed by oversight, so every interface build left
# 660 KB of churn in `git status` and the tracked copy drifted from the generator
# that owns it. Both are build outputs now, and `verify-build-order.mjs` checks
# that every entry point builds them before anything that needs them runs.
ui/studio.html
ui/studio-core.html

# local test dependency for the boot test
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# tauri
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/icons/

# Test output. Both suites write here - `shoot.mjs` the page shots, `drive.mjs`
# the gesture shots - so this is generated on every run and committing it would
# put three megabytes of churn in every test commit. Regenerate with:
#     node ui/test/shoot.mjs http://127.0.0.1:7878 shots
#     node ui/test/drive.mjs http://127.0.0.1:7878 shots/drive
shots/

# Local scratch that predates the repository. Kept on disk, kept out of history
# until someone decides what it is.
.p1.py

# The server's own stdout when it is started with a redirect, which is how
# `start.sh` and the launch instructions run it. It is a live log of the running
# process, not a source file.
studio-run*.log

# the gate's own transcript, written by scripts/build.sh when it is redirected
.build.log

# The build cache forgen writes beside the sources. Regenerated on every build.
.forgen_cache/

# written into the open workspace by the Generate panel when no file is open
# (the panel creates and opens generated.dtr to append into)
generated.dtr
